1. What is a Solaris Zone?

A Solaris Zone is an isolated environment (mini server) created inside one Solaris operating system.

Think of it as creating multiple independent servers on one physical server.

2. Real-life example

Imagine you own a 3 BHK flat.

There is:

One electricity connection
One water connection
One building

But you divide it into 3 separate rooms.

Room 1 → Rahul
Room 2 → Ahmed
Room 3 → Priya

Each person:

Has their own key
Keeps their own belongings
Cannot interfere with the others

The whole flat is one building, but each room works independently.

A Solaris Zone works in the same way.

3. Without Zones

Suppose a company has three applications:

Payroll
Banking
HR

Without Zones:

Application 1
Application 2
Application 3
---------------------
Solaris OS
---------------------
Physical Server

If the Payroll application crashes or consumes all the memory, the Banking and HR applications may affected.

4. With Zones

Now the administrator creates three Zones.

Payroll Zone
----------------

Banking Zone
----------------

HR Zone
----------------

Global Zone
----------------

Physical Server

Each application runs in its own Zone.

If the Payroll Zone crashes,

Banking Zone keeps running.

HR Zone keeps running.

5. What is the Global Zone?

The Global Zone is the main (parent) Zone.

It is created automatically when Solaris is installed.

The Global Zone is used to:

Create new Zones
Delete Zones
Start and stop Zones
Allocate CPU and memory
Monitor all Zones

Think of it as the administrator's control room.

6. What are Non-Global Zones?

The Zones you create are called Non-Global Zones.

Example:

Global Zone
   |
-------------------------
| HR | Finance | Testing |

Each one is a Non-Global Zone.

Users inside one Zone cannot access another Zone unless specifically allowed.

7. Why do companies use Zones?
a) Security

Suppose an attacker gets access to the HR Zone.

They cannot directly access the Finance Zone because both Zones are isolated.

b) Better Resource Usage

Instead of buying three physical servers,

A company buys one powerful server and creates three Zones.

Example:

Server

|
|---- Zone1
|---- Zone2
|---- Zone3

This saves:

Hardware cost
Electricity
Rack space

7. Is a Zone the same as VMware?

Not exactly.

a) VMware
Physical Server

|
VM1 (Own OS)

VM2 (Own OS)

VM3 (Own OS)

Each VM has its own operating system and kernel

b) Solaris Zones
Physical Server

|

Solaris Kernel

|

Zone1

Zone2

Zone3

All Zones share the same Solaris kernel.

This makes Zones:

Faster
Lighter
Use less memory
Start quickly

